<title>CANADA: Loewen says two more states probe bid.</title>
<headline>Loewen says two more states probe bid.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loewen Group Inc said that two more states -- Washington and Oregon -- are examining anti-trust issues related to Service Corp International's US$2.9 billion takeover bid for Loewen.</p>
<p>Service is North America's biggest operator of funeral homes and cemeteries,while Loewen is its closest competitor.</p>
<p>Loewen said that seven other states, the U.S. Federal Trade Commission and Canada's Competition Bureau were also scrutinizing the deal.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
</text>
